<edge source="iran_houthi_escalation::shipping_operating_costs" target="global_financial_stress::corporate_spread_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising per-voyage costs (insurance, fuel, rerouting) raise input and working-capital costs for trade-exposed firms, worsening credit metrics and leading investors to demand wider corporate credit spreads.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_houthi_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_houthi_escalation::shipping_operating_costs" target="north_korea_nuclear::cross_border_cap_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher insurance premiums, rerouting and security surcharges materially raise transaction and logistics costs for exporters and project sponsors, causing private investors and funds to scale back or delay cross‑border capital commitments into technology and energy projects (including those channels that can be repurposed for DPRK procurement).</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_houthi_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">north_korea_nuclear</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_houthi_escalation::shipping_operating_costs" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::semiconductor_fab_capaci" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained higher insurance, diversion and transit costs for specialized equipment and chemical inputs raises lead times and supply shortages for fabs, forcing lower wafer starts and temporary curtailment of advanced production capacity.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_houthi_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
