<edge source="iran_houthi_escalation::sanctions_intensity" target="global_financial_stress::market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Expanded sanctions reduce correspondent-banking links and constrain market-makers' ability to intermediate cross-border bond trades, causing dealers to pull back and reducing observable bond-market liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_houthi_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_houthi_escalation::sanctions_intensity" target="global_financial_stress::corporate_spread_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter sanctions increase counterparty, settlement and trade-risk for internationally active firms (and their banks), reducing access to funding and increasing perceived default risk, which pushes corporate spreads wider.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_houthi_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_houthi_escalation::sanctions_intensity" target="north_korea_nuclear::cross_border_cap_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger and more rigorously enforced sanctions against Iran/Houthi-related entities prompt correspondent banks and institutional investors to de‑risk by withdrawing or restricting foreign capital exposures, reducing net cross‑border flows into sectors and intermediaries that could be exploited by DPRK networks.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_houthi_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">north_korea_nuclear</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_houthi_escalation::sanctions_intensity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalation of sanctions tied to Iran/Houthi activity prompts the US and allies to broaden and more tightly enforce export‑control licensing and entity lists to prevent sanction circumvention and dual‑use flows — including preemptive restrictions that affect China‑linked supply chains.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_houthi_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
