<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::conflict_intensity" target="global_financial_stress::corporate_spread_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in overall combat intensity increases operational interruptions, counterparty risk and default probability for firms (especially in Europe and energy‑sensitive sectors), so investors demand higher credit spreads on corporate bonds.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::conflict_intensity" target="iran_houthi_escalation::shipping_operating_costs" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">A marked increase in overall Russia–Ukraine kinetic intensity raises global maritime and geopolitical risk premia and prompts insurers and war‑risk underwriters to lift premiums and require more costly security measures, directly increasing per‑voyage operating costs for carriers in adjacent and global routes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_houthi_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::conflict_intensity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::semiconductor_fab_capaci" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating conflict disrupts production and logistics of critical inputs (e.g., semiconductor‑grade neon, specialty gases, transport routes) originating in or routed through the conflict region, causing downtime and reduced effective output at advanced fabs globally.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::conflict_intensity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::cross_border_transfer" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising conflict intensity raises commercial and compliance risk (insurance, sanctions exposure, due diligence burdens), prompting firms, universities and intermediaries to curtail or delay cross‑border transfers of technology, tooling and tacit expertise to higher‑risk foreign partners including Chinese entities.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
