  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Raised policy rates in major economies reduce near-term demand expectations for oil and increase the discount rate applied to future cash flows, exerting downward pressure on benchmark crude prices within months.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_financial_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_houthi_escalation</data>
