  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher policy rates raise sovereign borrowing costs and near‑term fiscal financing pressures, making governments more reluctant or slower to approve new defense appropriations and external aid tranches for the war.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_financial_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
